# CODEOWNERS — WP-529 Ф21 (see the WP-529 red-team enforcement design
# record in this project's governance history)
#
# Protects the files a PR author could otherwise edit to weaken or bypass
# their own attestation check: the digest/signing scripts, the schema they
# validate against, this file itself, and — critically — ALL workflows, not
# just attestation-*.yml. A narrower `attestation-*.yml`-only pattern would
# leave a PR free to add a brand-new workflow with `id-token: write` +
# `attestations: write` and mint its own competing attestation without any
# review (peer-session 2026-08-27-14-wp529-f21-implement-attestation, turn
# 7: "downstream-проверка не привязана криптографически к конкретному
# workflow identity" — until it is, every workflow file is part of this
# trust boundary, not only the two that happen to be named attestation-*).
#
# Also protects the red-team policy file whose digest gets signed into the
# attestation (.claude/skills/iwe-platform-redteam/SKILL.md) — a PR could
# otherwise weaken the policy itself and have that weaker policy attested
# without review.
#
# Enforcement requires "Require review from Code Owners" enabled in branch
# protection for `main` (Settings → Branches) — this file alone does not
# block anything.
#
# Starting list is the repo owner only, per DRR "Круг проверяющих" decision
# (2026-08-27) — expand explicitly as trusted auditors are added, do not
# widen silently.

/.github/CODEOWNERS                        @TserenTserenov
/.github/workflows/**                      @TserenTserenov
/scripts/attestation-*.sh                  @TserenTserenov
/scripts/attestation-*.schema.json         @TserenTserenov
/.claude/skills/iwe-platform-redteam/SKILL.md @TserenTserenov
